    {
      "text": "# DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash: Pushing the Limits of KV Cache Compression",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "We introduce **DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash**, a multimodal Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model with 552B backbone parameters and support for contexts of up to one million tokens.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "**Architecture.** DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash adopts a **Causal Encoder-Decoder (CED)** architecture: a 40-layer Transformer organized as a 20-layer causal encoder followed by a 20-layer decoder.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "This allows the model to activate only **8B parameters per token during prefill** and **16B during decode**, substantially improving cost efficiency for input-heavy agentic workloads.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "**SWA Bounded Replay** reconstructs missing SWA KV states by replaying only the most recent *n*_win tokens, avoiding the need to persist SWA KV to SSD and reducing the persistent KV cache footprint to roughly **1/8** of that of DeepSeek-V4-Flash.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "**Compressed Sparse Attention 2 (CSA2).** DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash uses CSA2, which assigns each attention layer one of three static modes — **Full**, **Reindex**, or **Reuse** — to share main KV and indexer K across layers and reuse Top-K sparse-attention indices.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combined with **FP4 main KV caching** (E2M1 format, one E4M3 scale per 16 channels), these designs reduce the global KV cache footprint to **890 bytes per token** — roughly **1/4** of DeepSeek-V4-Flash.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "The model uses 1 shared expert and 384 routed experts per MoE layer, activating 6 routed experts per token.",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
      "publisher": "Hugging Face · deepseek-ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "Evaluating DeepSeek V4.1 Flash-1017 for loss of control and harmful manipulation risks",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35671",
      "publisher": "arXiv"
    },
    {
      "text": "To address this gap, we present an independent safety evaluation of DeepSeek V4.1 Flash-1017, the latest version of V4.1 Flash that departs from V4 with a new architecture, scaled-up training, and strong agentic capabilities.",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35671",
      "publisher": "arXiv"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drawing on the EU General-Purpose AI Code of Practice, we evaluate the model across 34 benchmarks, including 5 in-house suites, spanning evaluation integrity, loss of control, and harmful manipulation.",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35671",
      "publisher": "arXiv"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conforming to the AEF-1 standard, we compare V4.1 Flash-1017 against V4.1 Flash, earlier DeepSeek V4 models, and leading closed-source systems (GPT-6 Astra, GPT-5.6 Sol, and Gemini 3.8 Flash).",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35671",
      "publisher": "arXiv"
    },
    {
      "text": "Overall, V4.1 Flash-1017 shows substantial safety improvements over the V4 generation and approaches or matches leading closed-source baselines on several dimensions, while still exhibiting notable behaviors that warrant continued attention.",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35671",
      "publisher": "arXiv"
    },
    {
      "text": "Published: 2026-10-26T16:14:17Z",
